X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Phone";ID=35516;TYPE=PhoneUS10NoExt:(828) 250
 -4260
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Notice - Description";ID=51963;TYPE=SingleLin
 e:Information about Open and Closed Parks
DTSTAMP:20250617T085331Z
DESCRIPTION:Email: parks@buncombecounty.org<br>Phone: (828) 250-4260<br>
 Notice - Description: Information about Open and Closed Parks<br><br>Man
 y Buncombe County Parks were impacted by Hurricane Helene.&#160\; While 
 we are working diligently reopen parks as quickly as we can\, some parks
  continue to remain closed. Please see the list below for which parks ar
 e open and which parks continue to be closed for safety reasons.<br><br>
 OPEN Parks:&#160\; Lake Julian Park (please note\, some disc golf holes 
 remain closed)\, Hominy Valley Park\, Collier Cove Nature Preserve\, Nor
 th Buncombe Fields\, Cane Creek Playground\, Buncombe County Sports Park
 \, Corcoran Paige River Park\, Bent Creek River Park\, Ledges Whitewater
  Park\, and Hominy Creek River Park.&#160\; If people choose to recreate
  on the river\, we strongly encourage them to be aware of changes on str
 eambanks and in the riverbed and the potential for unknown debris from H
 elene.<br><br>CLOSED Parks:&#160\; Charles D. Owen Park\, Karpen Soccer 
 Field\, Alexander River Park\, Walnut Island River Park\, and Glen Bridg
 e River Park*. *Note\, if the gate is open at Glen Bridge River Park\, i
 t may be used.&#160\; For safety reasons\, we ask the public not to ente
 r closed parks.<br><br>Please email <a href="mailto:parks@buncombecounty
 .org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">parks@buncombecounty.org</a> or cal
 l (828) 250-4260 with any questions or for additional information.
CATEGORIES:Parks &amp; Recreation
UID:http://uid.trumba.com/event/179136489
X-TRUMBA-LINK:https://www.buncombecounty.org/countycenter/events-calenda
 r.aspx?trumbaEmbed=view%3Devent%26eventid%3D179136489
END:VEVENT
